  "term": "schwannoma",
  "definition": "A schwannoma is a noncancerous, usually enclosed, slow-growing tumor made up of Schwann cells. It occurs in peripheral or cranial nerves and tends to come back only rarely, with malignant change reported only in uncommon cases.",
